The [[☃ definition 2]] will pass through points $(1,f(1))$ and $(5,f(5))$.

$\begin{align}
\text{slope}&=\dfrac{\text{change in }y}{\text{change in }x}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{f(5)-f(1)}{5-1}
\end{align}$

![Function f is graphed. The x-axis goes from negative 1 to 6. The graph is a curve. The curve starts in quadrant 2, moves upward with increasing steepness, through a point at (1, f of 1) and (5, f of 5), and ends in quadrant 1. A secant line connects the 2 points.](web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/5d377b2aa9b3e742d1a6d573f2795057abdea161)

We will need to know the values of $f(1)$ and $f(5)$ to find the slope.

$\begin{align}
f(1)&=0.5^{-1}
\\\\
&=2
\\\\
f(5)&=0.5^{-5}
\\\\
&=32
\end{align}$

Now we can find the slope:

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{f(5)-f(1)}{5-1}&=\dfrac{32-2}{4}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{15}{2}
\end{align}$
